          ],
          "text": "On admission, blood glucose was HI (meter high), ketones 5.2, pH 7.18, HCO3 11, and glucose 34, confirming severe DKA. PICU was informed and she was managed on the ward HDU. She was treated with the DKA protocol: cautious IV fluids, fixed-rate insulin infusion, potassium replacement, and hourly monitoring. By Day 2, pH had improved to 7.34 and ketones to 0.8. She was subsequently transitioned to subcutaneous insulin on a basal-bolus regimen. Diabetes nurse and dietician input commenced, with family education begun covering carbohydrate counting, hypo management, and sick-day rules.",
